<!--
     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
     Copyright 2026 The DiamaneOS Project

     Device corrections to the stock carrier data. CarrierConfig reads this
     file last, after the carrier's own file and the stock vendor.xml, so a
     value here applies to every carrier.

     world_phone_bool: the stock vendor.xml sets it for every carrier, a
     Qualcomm default for CDMA world phones. With it, Settings drops the
     network-type list GrapheneOS shows ("5G", "4G", "LTE only", "5G only",
     filtered by what the modem supports) for an unfiltered list of 34 modes,
     CDMA, EvDo and TD-SCDMA included, and adds CDMA system-select options.
     No carrier file sets it and the Android default is false. It changes
     what Settings offers (and TelephonyManager.isWorldPhone), not radio or
     emergency behaviour.
-->
<carrier_config_list>
    <carrier_config>
        <boolean name="world_phone_bool" value="false" />
    </carrier_config>
</carrier_config_list>
